# Restora Mobile - environment example
#
# NO .env variable is required for ordinary local development with defaults.
# Expo project linkage is COMMITTED in app.json:
#   expo.owner = ubaidbadar333
#   expo.extra.eas.projectId = d70f9478-a188-4e8d-9faf-dad5de802bbd
# Do NOT set EAS_PROJECT_ID in GitHub Actions; EAS reads app.json automatically.
#
# REQUIRED OUTSIDE .env FOR AUTOMATIC GITHUB APK/IPA BUILDS:
#   GitHub Actions SECRET: EXPO_TOKEN (Expo account access token).
#   EAS Android signing credentials must be initialized interactively once.
#   iOS device IPA: paid Apple Developer membership, registered devices, and
#   EAS iOS signing credentials initialized interactively once.
#
# REQUIRED OUTSIDE .env FOR THE SEPARATE GOOGLE PLAY RELEASE WORKFLOW
# (pushes to main and stage ONLY):
#   GitHub Secrets: GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON, ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64,
#                   KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, KEY_ALIAS, KEY_PASSWORD.
#   GitHub variable EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is optional (defaults to https://restora.live).
#   The Play workflow builds an AAB using Gradle, not EAS Build.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are baked into the app and are NOT secrets.
# For hosted EAS preview builds, configure them in the EAS "preview" environment.
#
# OPTIONAL - backend API URL:
#   Local dev default: http://<Metro-host>:5001
#   Release default: https://restora.live
#   Use HTTPS for production builds.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# RECOMMENDED FOR RELEASE BUILDS that need "Open Restora on the web":
#   Current fallback is http://<Metro-host>:3000 even in release builds.
#   Set your actual web app URL (example: https://app.restora.live).
EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=

# OPTIONAL - public site for guest table QR codes. Default: https://restora.live
EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# OPTIONAL - Google sign-in. Leave blank to hide Google sign-in.
# The Web client ID should match the backend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.
# The iOS client ID needs to match the app's iOS bundle identifier.
# Android also needs a Google Cloud Android OAuth client with the signing SHA-1.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=

# OPTIONAL - Android notifications: path to Firebase google-services.json.
# For GitHub Play builds, supply its CONTENTS using the GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON
# Actions secret (the workflow writes a temporary file).
# For EAS builds, set up a file environment variable / build credentials in Expo.
# iOS notifications require an APNs key in Expo credentials instead.
GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON=

# BACKEND ONLY - NOT USED BY THIS MOBILE APP OR ITS BUILD WORKFLOWS:
#   EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN (authenticates your backend's Expo push requests, if enabled)
#   WEB_PUSH_PUBLIC_KEY / WEB_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY (browser VAPID keys)
# Keep these in restora-backend's environment; don't copy them here.
